---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="QA Items Assignment and Resolution Guidelines">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Get Started — Develop"
    title="QA Items Assignment and Resolution Guidelines"
    description="Guidelines to simplify and clarify the collection, identification, and assignment of QA items."
  />

  <section class="sec">
    <h2>Guidelines</h2>
    <p class="body-text">
      This guideline aims to provide guidance and to simplify with clarity the collection, identification, and
      assignment of QA items by the QA to the developer. QA items are issues raised after a Development Change.
      Development Changes can be new application or additional features. QA items can be sourced from a QA, client,
      and/or any concerned party.
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
      Once QA items are received, a QA file must be created. QA file should reside to a directory local to its
      project workspace and agreed upon by involved parties. A QA file should only contain items specific to the
      project. It should follow the following conventions:
    </p>

    <h3>File Format and Tab Structure</h3>
    <h4>Filename</h4>
    <p class="body-text">
      <strong>Format:</strong> QA-Project Name-Version<br />
      <strong>Example:</strong> QA-eBilling-2.0
    </p>

    <h4>Tabs</h4>
    <p class="body-text">
      <strong>Tabname:</strong> Current Project Version
    </p>
    <h5>Version</h5>
    <h6>Major version</h6>
    <ul class="body-text">
      <li>This requires a new QA file spreadsheet</li>
    </ul>
    <h6>Minor version</h6>
    <ul class="body-text">
      <li>New tab from the major version of the QA file</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Columns</h4>
    <p class="body-text">This are the required columns for the QA file.</p>
    <ul class="body-text">
      <li>Function</li>
      <li>Sub-Function</li>
      <li>Description of Feedback/Issues</li>
      <li>Screenshot</li>
      <li>Remarks</li>
      <li>Assigned To</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Updating</h3>
    <p class="body-text">Assignment of items are agreed upon the team</p>
    <p class="body-text">Once items are assigned, developers should follow the following steps</p>

    <h3>Color Coding Standard</h3>
    <p class="body-text">Below is the color scheme for updating the status of items in the QA file</p>
    <ul class="body-text">
      <li><strong>White/No Color:</strong> Indicates an OPEN item</li>
      <li><strong>Orange:</strong> Indicates an item that is currently ON GOING fix by the developer</li>
      <li><strong>Green:</strong> Indicates a PASSED item</li>
      <li><strong>Red:</strong> Denotes a FAILED item</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sec { margin-bottom: 72px; }

  .sec h2 {
    font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.4px; color: var(--black);
    margin-bottom: 24px; padding-bottom: 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--g5);
  }

  .sec h3 {
    font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.3px; color: var(--black);
    margin-top: 36px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .sec h4 {
    font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.2px; color: var(--black);
    margin-top: 28px; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .sec h5 {
    font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.1px; color: var(--black);
    margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .sec h6 {
    font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black);
    margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .body-text {
    font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--g1); line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .body-text strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .body-text ul {
    list-style: disc;
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .body-text ul li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
